From: egui-aros
Subject: [PATCH] aros-gui-sys: open gl.library on request, not at program start

Repository: aros-development-team/AROS bf7075aab8480cf36bdc13b4382ccbd6098c8a0d,
  tools/crosstools/rust/crates/aros-gui-sys.
Date: 2026-10-28
Problem: gl.c pulled in libGL's autoinit, so every program linking the GL
  glue opened gl.library (and with it Mesa) at start, even when it then drew
  with the CPU. Mesa starts a helper process on the first open; it inherits a
  copy of the opener's home directory and keeps it while gl.library stays
  loaded, so the program's drawer stayed "in use" after the program had
  ended (VectorCraft on ABIv11 2026.09, pool v11-3: a "New Process" with the
  program drawer as home dir remained; the drawer could not be deleted until
  a reboot; the CLI, which does not link the GL glue, left nothing).
Rationale: GLBase is defined here, so the linker leaves libGL's autoinit
  object (gl_autoinit.o, the only definition of GLBase in libGL.a) out.
  aros_gui_gl_open() opens gl.library version 20 (the stubs' libreq) with the
  caller's home and current directory cleared for the call, and
  aros_gui_gl_close() closes it. A program that never asks for OpenGL never
  opens gl.library.
Scope: two functions and the GLBase definition; callers must call
  aros_gui_gl_open() before creating a context (egui-aros does, in its GL path).
Upstream-status: candidate for mainline's crate store (same change applies);
  not submitted.
---
diff --color -ruN aros-gui-sys-0.1.0.orig/src/gl.c aros-gui-sys-0.1.0/src/gl.c
--- aros-gui-sys-0.1.0.orig/src/gl.c	2026-10-28 20:21:02
+++ aros-gui-sys-0.1.0/src/gl.c	2026-10-28 20:21:02
@@ -1,8 +1,11 @@
 /* gl.library's GLA context for Rust on AROS. Contract: glue.h.
 
-   A separate object from glue.c, so only programs that use GL pull in
-   libGL's autoinit, which opens gl.library at startup. */
+   gl.library is opened by aros_gui_gl_open(), when a program decides to use
+   OpenGL, not by libGL's autoinit at program start: GLBase is defined here,
+   so the linker leaves libGL's autoinit object out. */
 #include <stdint.h>
+#include <proto/exec.h>
+#include <proto/dos.h>
 #include <intuition/intuition.h>
 #include <utility/tagitem.h>
 #include <GL/gla.h>
@@ -17,6 +20,35 @@
 #define GLA_PROFILE_COMPAT      0
 #define GLA_PROFILE_CORE        1
 #endif
+
+struct Library *GLBase = NULL;
+
+/* gl.library starts helper processes (Mesa's threads) on its first open and
+   keeps them while it stays loaded. A process inherits a copy of the opener's
+   home and current directory, which would keep the program's drawer "in use"
+   after the program has ended; the opener's are cleared for the open. */
+int aros_gui_gl_open(void)
+{
+    BPTR home, current;
+
+    if (GLBase)
+        return 1;
+    home = SetProgramDir(BNULL);
+    current = CurrentDir(BNULL);
+    GLBase = OpenLibrary("gl.library", 20);
+    CurrentDir(current);
+    SetProgramDir(home);
+    return GLBase != NULL;
+}
+
+void aros_gui_gl_close(void)
+{
+    if (GLBase)
+    {
+        CloseLibrary(GLBase);
+        GLBase = NULL;
+    }
+}
 
 /* The window interior, which is what the context renders into. */
 static void set_rast_tags(struct TagItem *tags, struct Window *window)
